   :pre-registration "Stated in checks/construct_cascade.clj before the run and executed on every -main, so the control arm cannot be dropped when it is inconvenient: the degree term is DISTINGUISHABLE FROM UNIFORM iff at least one construction admits a different pattern, or stops at a different point, than the same construction with degree forced to zero. Secondary: the share of scored candidates with degree > 0 at step 0."
   :method "checks/construct_cascade.clj -main, over library/ whole (98 sections, 1239 patterns, 92 authored @why edges, 124 @why+@how). Tension :organise-the-library, four clauses cited from futon2/holes/problems/P-organise-the-library.md:33-36 and :5-6 and :57-58, each with authored literal cues. Seed 9 (the patterns whose IF and HOWEVER each acknowledge some clause), 50 scored candidates. alpha 0.3 (cascade_construct.py:206), budget 20 (cascade_serve.py:21-27). Report checks/construct-cascade.edn (sha256 fa644053365fd05c43faa253ffff0b2fe7a8fe73d7a32f95d55c15c517cb4abd), commit futon3 d73c4d5."
   :result "DISTINGUISHABLE. Under :widen-to-a-budget, 2 of 11 admissions change when the degree term is removed (data-mining/gates-as-code and data-mining/saturate-the-accelerator-with-concurrency in the uniform arm; snatch/play-the-authored-order-first and snatch/promote-the-remedy-before-the-exit in the real one). Under :widen-to-the-marginal-gain-floor the real arm admits 4 and the uniform arm admits NONE, because with degree 0 the best score is 3*0.3 = 0.9 and epsilon is 1.0. The budget arm settles it WITHOUT the floor -- recorded separately as :distinguishable-without-the-floor?, because epsilon is a threshold this file chose and the budget is one the operator ruled, so a verdict resting only on epsilon would be the weaker claim."
   :and-thinly "4 of 50 scored candidates have any degree at all, every one of them exactly 1, and all four are in library/cascades and library/snatch -- the two sections a person organised by hand (:sections-supplying-the-degree-term). So the term discriminates where the library is organised and is flat over the other 46. The cost :constructor-relevance-substrate stated is now measured rather than predicted: the constructor does not become good by being written, it becomes good as L5/L9 land."
   :does-not-redirect-to-L5-L9 "The :changes-it condition is NOT met, so the interim arm :authored-edge-degree stands and LA4-LA9 are not blocked on coverage. What the measurement does say is that a cascade constructed today is a cascade over the organised sections plus whatever the text matcher drags in, which is a bound to state on any LA4-LA9 result rather than a reason to stop."
