   :decision "A cue must OCCUR, case-insensitively, IN ITS OWN CLAUSE'S CITED SPAN of the source record, re-read from disk on every run. checks/construct_zaif_cascade.clj `cue-licence` checks it and an unlicensed cue is a hard failure, not a warning."
   :it-is-a-removal-rule-only "The licence strikes cues; it never suggests one. A cue added after a run is tuning whatever it is called, and no cue was added to LA5's tension after its first run. This asymmetry is the whole discipline: a rule that could also add would let an author widen the seed by widening the clause."
   :effect "seed 38 -> 11, candidates 457 -> 343, sections 25 -> 8. The reviewer-named falsifier is no longer selected. The budget temperament stopped being degenerate as a side effect (seed 11 < budget 20, so it admits 9 rather than halting at step 0)."
